      "id": "claim_752df5508f6c4a998b11e3b177d358bd",
      "statement": "A WUX stores a WUD's bytes losslessly: a 32-byte little-endian header with the WUX0 magic and a 0x8000 sector size, a u32 table naming the stored sector for each disc sector, then each distinct sector once in first-use order; wux_rs::compress and decompress convert between the two.",
